# The compiler's line of the refusal starts with the header's path on the machine, so the message is
# a contains: line. wasip2 and wasip3 have the same message in a compile-diagnostic
# (test/messages/chacha_default_not_linked); compile-diagnostic is clang's and skips Emscripten, so
# this fixture is the Emscripten one.
[all]
targets: emscripten
build: fails
# tag::messages[]
contains: webcpp::crypto: ChaCha20-Poly1305's default backend on this target is libsodium, which is not linked. Add /webcpp/crypto//chacha20_poly1305-default, the default's library on every target, to the program's Jamfile, as in: exe app : app.cpp /webcpp/crypto//crypto /webcpp/crypto//chacha20_poly1305-default ; or name another backend in the type, as in ciphers::chacha20_poly1305<backends::bearssl>. The backends that have it: sodium (native, wasip2, wasip3, emscripten), bearssl (native, wasip2, wasip3, emscripten), openssl (native, wasip2, wasip3). (without b2: define WEBCPP_CRYPTO_HAS_SODIUM=1 and link libsodium built with webcpp's src/canary_sodium.c)
contains: webcpp::crypto: original ChaCha20-Poly1305's default backend on this target is libsodium, which is not linked, and the one backend that has it there. Add /webcpp/crypto//chacha20_poly1305_original-default, the default's library on every target, to the program's Jamfile, as in: exe app : app.cpp /webcpp/crypto//crypto /webcpp/crypto//chacha20_poly1305_original-default ; (without b2: define WEBCPP_CRYPTO_HAS_SODIUM=1 and link libsodium built with webcpp's src/canary_sodium.c)
contains: webcpp::crypto: XChaCha20-Poly1305's default backend on this target is libsodium, which is not linked, and the one backend that has it there. Add /webcpp/crypto//xchacha20_poly1305-default, the default's library on every target, to the program's Jamfile, as in: exe app : app.cpp /webcpp/crypto//crypto /webcpp/crypto//xchacha20_poly1305-default ; (without b2: define WEBCPP_CRYPTO_HAS_SODIUM=1 and link libsodium built with webcpp's src/canary_sodium.c)
# end::messages[]
